4. Setup Instructions
4.1 Clone the Repo
git clone https://github.com/rishit911/file_vault_app.git file_vault_proj
cd file_vault_proj

4.2 Environment Variables

Create a local .env file in backend/:

DATABASE_URL=postgres://filevault_user:Pguk2814%409R@localhost:5433/filevault_db?sslmode=disable
JWT_SECRET=supersecretdevkey_local
PORT=8080
STORAGE_PATH=/data/files


⚠️ Replace %409R with URL encoding of @ in your password.

Do not commit .env. Only .env.example is in git.

4.3 Run PostgreSQL (via Docker)
cd infra
docker compose up -d postgres


Check connection:

psql -h localhost -p 5433 -U filevault_user filevault_db

4.4 Run Migrations

Install migrate CLI and run:

migrate -path backend/migrations -database "postgres://filevault_user:Pguk2814%409R@localhost:5433/filevault_db?sslmode=disable" up

4.5 Start Backend
cd backend
go run ./cmd/server


Test health check:

curl http://localhost:8080/health
# Expected: "OK"

4.6 Start Frontend
cd frontend
npm install
npm run dev


Open: http://localhost:3000

5. Database Schema
Tables

users

id UUID PK

email TEXT UNIQUE

password_hash TEXT

role TEXT (default=user)

created_at TIMESTAMP

file_objects

id UUID PK

hash TEXT UNIQUE

storage_path TEXT

size_bytes BIGINT

mime_type TEXT

ref_count INT

created_at TIMESTAMP

user_files

id UUID PK

user_id FK → users.id

file_object_id FK → file_objects.id

filename TEXT

visibility TEXT (private/public)

uploaded_at TIMESTAMP

shares

id UUID PK

user_file_id FK → user_files.id

public_link TEXT

expires_at TIMESTAMP

download_count BIGINT

created_at TIMESTAMP

downloads

id UUID PK

user_file_id FK → user_files.id

downloader_ip TEXT

downloaded_at TIMESTAMP

6. API Endpoints
6.1 Health

GET /health
✅ Returns "OK" if backend is running.

6.2 Authentication
Register

POST /api/v1/auth/register
Request:

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123!"
}


Response:

{
  "id": "uuid-of-user"
}

Login

POST /api/v1/auth/login
Request:

{
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "Secret123!"
}


Response:

{
  "token": "<jwt-token>"
}

6.3 Files
Register Metadata (Deduplication Skeleton)

POST /api/v1/files/register
Headers:
X-User-Id: <uuid> (temporary, until JWT middleware added)

Request:

{
  "filename": "sample.pdf",
  "hash": "sha256-hash",
  "size_bytes": 1024,
  "mime_type": "application/pdf"
}


Response:

{
  "file_object_id": "uuid",
  "user_file_id": "uuid"
}

